{"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity","doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/GraphProtocols"]]},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/isOuterplanar","doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/isPlanar"],"title":"Instance Properties","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/findKuratowskiSubgraph()","doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/planarEmbedding()"],"title":"Instance Methods","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/planarity\/graphprotocols\/graph"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"extension"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P","kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"title":"Graph","modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"Planarity"}],"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:e:s:14GraphProtocols0A0P9PlanarityE16_planarEdgeLimitSivp","roleHeading":"Extended Protocol","symbolKind":"extension"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Planarity on undirected graphs. Self-loops and parallel edges never change an answer: the tests"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"run on the underlying simple graph, read once through the rows in index space. A directed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"graph’s planarity is that of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"graph.undirected"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"extension","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P","text":"Graph","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isPlanar"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"planarEmbedding()"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isOuterplanar"},{"type":"text","text":" run the left-right planarity test (de"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Fraysseix and Rosenstiehl, in Brandes’s formulation, 2009); "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"findKuratowskiSubgraph()"},{"type":"text","text":" runs"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Boyer and Myrvold’s edge-addition algorithm (2004), whose failure state isolates the witness."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"All are O(n + m), iterative, and deterministic: graphs with the same rows (the same vertices in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the same order, the same edge positions, the same incidence order) get the same embedding and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the same witness."}]}]}],"references":{"doc://Planarity/documentation/Planarity/GraphProtocols/Graph/isOuterplanar":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"isOuterplanar","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/isOuterplanar","title":"isOuterplanar","url":"\/documentation\/planarity\/graphprotocols\/graph\/isouterplanar","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Whether the graph has a planar embedding with every vertex on one face (Mathematica’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OuterplanarGraphQ"},{"type":"text","text":"): whether the graph plus a new vertex joined to every vertex is planar."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A simple graph with more than 2n − 3 edges is not. O(n + m)."}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"title":"Graph","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"abstract":[{"text":"An undirected graph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of undirected edges","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"between them. Kept apart from ","type":"text"},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": an undirected graph is not a symmetric directed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one, and no type is both. ","type":"text"},{"code":"directed","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" views it as one when an algorithm needs arcs.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graph","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Planarity/documentation/Planarity/GraphProtocols":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/GraphProtocols","title":"GraphProtocols","url":"\/documentation\/planarity\/graphprotocols","abstract":[],"role":"collection"},"doc://Planarity/documentation/Planarity":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/planarity","title":"Planarity","abstract":[],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity","role":"collection"},"doc://Planarity/documentation/Planarity/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"title":"Graph","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Planarity on undirected graphs. Self-loops and parallel edges never change an answer: the tests","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"run on the underlying simple graph, read once through the rows in index space. A directed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"graph’s planarity is that of ","type":"text"},{"code":"graph.undirected","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/planarity\/graphprotocols\/graph","fragments":[{"text":"extension","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Planarity/documentation/Planarity/GraphProtocols/Graph/isPlanar":{"url":"\/documentation\/planarity\/graphprotocols\/graph\/isplanar","identifier":"doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/isPlanar","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"isPlanar","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Whether the graph can be drawn in the plane without crossing edges (NetworkX’s "},{"code":"is_planar","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Boost’s "},{"code":"boyer_myrvold_planarity_test","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"). A simple graph with more than 3n − 6 edges is not,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which is answered after counting distinct pairs, before any search. O(n + m)."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"isPlanar"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://Planarity/documentation/Planarity/GraphProtocols/Graph/findKuratowskiSubgraph()":{"title":"findKuratowskiSubgraph()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A subdivision of K₅ or K₃,₃ made of the graph’s edges, or nil when the graph is planar: the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"witness of non-planarity (Boost’s "},{"code":"kuratowski_subgraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", JGraphT’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"getKuratowskiSubdivision()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"). A dense graph is searched on its first 3n − 5 distinct pairs"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only, which already hold one. O(n + m)."}],"url":"\/documentation\/planarity\/graphprotocols\/graph\/findkuratowskisubgraph()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"findKuratowskiSubgraph","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:9Planarity18KuratowskiSubgraphV","text":"KuratowskiSubgraph","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">?","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/findKuratowskiSubgraph()","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Planarity/documentation/Planarity/GraphProtocols/Graph/planarEmbedding()":{"url":"\/documentation\/planarity\/graphprotocols\/graph\/planarembedding()","identifier":"doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/planarEmbedding()","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"planarEmbedding()","abstract":[{"text":"A planar embedding of the graph, over every edge position (loops and parallel copies","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"included), or nil when the graph is not planar: the witness of planarity (NetworkX’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"check_planarity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", Boost’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"embedding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" output). O(n + m), faces included.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"planarEmbedding"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:9Planarity15PlanarEmbed